## Mockups (non-negotiable — read before building frames)

Applies to Chat tasks, Chat Assist, APD, Care Plans, and every other app example:

1. **Existing tokens only** — bind radius, spacing, color, elevation. Never type raw Corner radius / gap / pad when a variable exists (e.g. `12` → **`radius/xl`**, not a hardcoded `12`).
2. **Existing text styles only** — Figtree via `body1` / `subtitle2` / `caption` / headings. No freehand fonts or unbound type scales.
3. **Existing library components only** — instance published masters; do not detach to restyle; do not invent new components or one-off patterns.
4. **Missing component / token / style → stop and prompt the user** before creating anything new. After they decide, note the gap in `open-items.md`. Never silently invent to unblock a mock.
5. **Before done:** linked-variable icons on radius/fill/spacing; text styles applied; chrome is live instances; no new component/token/style without explicit go-ahead.

Full checklist: `component-notes.md` → **Mockups / app examples**.
